<title>JAPAN: JAL to start Kansai-Rome service.</title>
<headline>JAL to start Kansai-Rome service.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan Airlines Co Ltd said on Friday it will start a new service from Kansai International Airport in western Japan to Rome via Milan, on November 2.</p>
<p>A JAL spokesman said a Transportation Ministry council approved the airline's registration for the service and issued a licence on September 19.</p>
<p>JAL will offer a twice-weekly service on the new route, using Boeing 747-400 aircraft, the spokesman said.</p>
</text>
